# VTID-04236 — commands run during this change

## Trigger: Morning Health Check reported check 11 FAIL
Morning Health Check: 3/21 FAILED
| 11 | DB-content locale coverage (GA languages) | FAIL |
  My Journey short: [{"locale":"tr","complete_rows":253,"expected":254}];
  Navigator short: [{"locale":"tr","complete_rows":282,"expected":291},
                     {"locale":"zh","complete_rows":289,"expected":291},
                     {"locale":"ar","complete_rows":290,"expected":291}]

## Root cause investigation — identified exact missing rows
$ SELECT canon.topic_id, jct.topic_id IS NOT NULL AS row_exists, ...
  FROM journey_checklist_translations canon LEFT JOIN ... WHERE locale='tr'
  -> T178 missing entirely for tr

$ SELECT sl_code, canon.catalog_id, nci.catalog_id IS NOT NULL AS row_exists, ...
  FROM nav_catalog_i18n canon LEFT JOIN ... WHERE lang IN ('tr','zh','ar')
  -> 12 missing rows: 766473da (ar+tr+zh), 2eaff461/3bab8e1f/a7f803f5/c588bc7c/
     c99a06f5/efa294ac/f7dd3022/f8764dac (tr only), ad180ad8 (zh only)

## Root cause of the tooling gap
$ cat scripts/journey/generate-checklist-translations.mjs
  -> calls Google Gemini API directly (GEMINI_API_KEY, generativelanguage.
     googleapis.com) — forbidden per CLAUDE.md ALWAYS 10a/10c, IF-THEN 27
     (no sanctioned Google dependency for LLM content generation).
  -> LOCALES allowlist hardcoded to ['en','es','sr'] — would silently drop
     tr/zh/ar even if invoked.
$ grep -rl "nav_catalog_i18n" scripts/ services/
  -> no backfill/translation script exists for nav_catalog_i18n at all.

## Fix 1 — rewrote scripts/journey/generate-checklist-translations.mjs
Replaced the Gemini HTTPS call with `aws bedrock-runtime invoke-model`
(model eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6, region eu-central-1 — the exact
invocation CLAUDE.md §2b documents as verified-invokable). Extended
SUPPORTED_LOCALES from ['en','es','sr'] to the full GA target set
(en,es,sr,fr,pl,pt,ru,tr,zh,ar).

$ node --check scripts/journey/generate-checklist-translations.mjs
exit: 0 (outputs/node-check-journey.txt)

## Fix 2 — new scripts/nav/generate-nav-catalog-translations.mjs
Same Bedrock-based approach, analogous to fix 1, for nav_catalog_i18n
(which has no separate source table — 'en' is used as the translation
source, per CLAUDE.md §3's own note that nav_catalog_i18n's 'en' rows are
the reference-coverage locale with full 291/291 parity).

$ node --check scripts/nav/generate-nav-catalog-translations.mjs
exit: 0 (outputs/node-check-nav.txt)

